        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113418,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113419,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most SPs occur in the hard palate, followed by the buccal mucosa. Other sites include the soft palate, tongue, mouth floor, parotid gland, bronchus, and oesophagus {33443864; 33712056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113420,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SP usually presents as a raised sessile or pedunculated mucosal lesion {33712056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113421,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SP is rare and tends to occur in older adults. The age range is 2&ndash;91&nbsp;years (median: 62&nbsp;years) {5353939; 28887760; 31473937}. There is a male predominance {33712056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113422,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113423,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p><em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutation is consistently reported in SP {31473937; 33443864}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:41:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113424,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SP is typically polypoid with a papillary surface and well-circumscribed margins. The size is usually &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm, and cystic spaces might be grossly visible on cut section {5353939; 28887760; 31473937; 33712056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113425,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>SP is characterized by the presence of both exophytic surface squamous and endophytic ductal papillary proliferation. The exophytic squamous proliferation is directly contiguous with submucosal salivary gland ductal epithelium that shows endophytic papillary infoldings and cystic-like spaces {5353939; 28887760; 31505033}. The ductal epithelium has a biphasic pattern, with luminal cuboidal or columnar cells and basally located basal cells {28887760}. A lymphoplasmacytic stromal infiltrate is common. The ductal luminal cells may show oncocytic metaplasia {31473937; 33712056}. Cases with endophytic ductal proliferation with <em>BRAF</em> mutation but no exophytic component are called &ldquo;SP-like intraductal papillary tumours&rdquo; {31505033}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The ductal cells are positive for CK7 and SOX10; the basal cells are positive for p63. The exophytic squamous cells are positive for p63 and CK13, and may be focally positive for CK7 {8887080; 31473937; 33712056}. Positive immunohistochemistry for BRAF p.V600E staining can be seen in both squamous and ductal components of SP {31505033; 33712056}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The presence of a typical exophytic and endophytic growth pattern can distinguish SP from other salivary duct papillary tumours including squamous cell papilloma, ductal papilloma, or cystadenoma. A lack of invasion and overt atypia distinguishes SP from adenosquamous carcinoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:41:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113426,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p>Not reported</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:42:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113427,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Demonstration of <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutation by PCR or other methods may be helpful.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113428,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> surface exophytic mucosal squamous proliferation and submucosal ductal cystic-like spaces.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> evidence of <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutation (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113429,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113430,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical removal is curative for SP. Recurrence and malignant transformation are very rare {33712056}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:16:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]